    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0606" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg594"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.248/55⅓</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-06">December 6, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Murray</hi>: I wish you would talk with Dr.
                    Berle and Mr. Philip Young regarding the matter dealt with in the attached
                        letter<anchor n="84" xml:id="d510-f1"/> from the Greek Minister. It is the
                    President’s most positive desire that these thirty planes be released to the
                    Greek Government. Surely some satisfactory way can be found of doing it.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d510-f1" n="84" xml:id="d510-f1-content">
